      "SecondaryAttribute": "User's Vague Prompt\n    \n      \"Environmental concerns occasionally surface in h...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 24px auto; line-height: 1.6;\">\n\n  <div style=\"background:#fff3cd; border:1px solid #f0c36d; border-radius:12px; padding:24px; margin-bottom:20px; box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); text-align:center;\">\n    <h2 style=\"color:#7a5c00; margin:0; font-size:22px;\">User's Vague Prompt</h2>\n    <p style=\"margin:10px 0 0; font-size:20px; font-weight:bold; color:#333;\">\n      \"Environmental concerns occasionally surface in heavily frequented places. (Popularity + Env. quality – broad surfacing)\"\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:10px; padding:20px; margin-bottom:24px;\">\n    <h3 style=\"color:#0f6cab; margin-top:0; font-size:18px;\">AI-Generated Chart Plan</h3>\n\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom:16px;\">\n      <p style=\"margin:0; font-weight:bold; font-size:16px;\">Popularity vs Environmental Quality by Region</p>\n      <p style=\"margin:2px 0; color:#555;\"><i>Multi-type chart</i></p>\n      <p style=\"margin:4px 0;\">The 'Popularity vs Environmental Quality by Region' chart gives a comparison of the average popularity score and environmental quality index for Region1, Region2, and Region3. This can help travelers choose regions that balance both their interests and environmental considerations.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom:16px;\">\n      <p style=\"margin:0; font-weight:bold; font-size:16px;\">Environmental Quality Trend by Quarter</p>\n      <p style=\"margin:2px 0; color:#555;\"><i>Line chart</i></p>\n      <p style=\"margin:4px 0;\">The 'Environmental Quality Trend by Quarter' line chart shows how the environmental quality index in Region1, Region2, and Region3 has changed over time. This can indicate the best times to visit these regions based on environmental factors.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom:16px;\">\n      <p style=\"margin:0; font-weight:bold; font-size:16px;\">Regional Review Distribution</p>\n      <p style=\"margin:2px 0; color:#555;\"><i>Pie chart</i></p>\n      <p style=\"margin:4px 0;\">The 'Regional Review Distribution' pie chart illustrates the proportion of reviews for Region1, Region2, and Region3. This can give travelers an idea of which regions are most frequently reviewed, potentially indicating popular or highly visited areas.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"margin-bottom:16px;\">\n      <p style=\"margin:0; font-weight:bold; font-size:16px;\">Safety vs Popularity Bubble Plot</p>\n      <p style=\"margin:2px 0; color:#555;\"><i>Bubble chart</i></p>\n      <p style=\"margin:4px 0;\">The 'Safety vs Popularity Bubble Plot' scatter chart shows the relationship between safety scores, popularity scores, and the volume of reviews for each region — Region1, Region2, and Region3. This can guide travelers in selecting regions that are both popular and safe, as indicated by larger bubbles.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>",
